choice
    prompt "MMU Page Size"
    default ARM64_PAGE_SIZE_4K
    help
        Select the page size for the ARM64 MMU. The default is 4KiB.
    depends on CONFIG_ARCH_AARCH64

    config ARM64_PAGE_SIZE_4K
        bool "4KiB"

    config ARM64_PAGE_SIZE_16K
        bool "16KiB"

    config ARM64_PAGE_SIZE_64K
        bool "64KiB"
endchoice
config KSHIM_IRQ
    bool "Interrupt-driven runtime (GICv3 and generic timer)"
    default y
    help
        Discover the GICv3 and the generic timer from the runtime device
        tree, take device and timer interrupts on the boot CPU, and sleep in
        WFI instead of busy-waiting. Interrupt state is restored before
        payload handoff. See docs/interrupts.md. Without it, or when the
        GIC cannot be brought up, the runtime polls as before.

config KSHIM_IRQ_SELFTEST
    bool "Run the QEMU interrupt self-test and exit"
    depends on KSHIM_IRQ && KSHIM_QEMU_PLATFORM && KSHIM_SMP
    default n
    help
        Seed a non-trivial inherited GIC state, then check timer interrupts
        and WFI idle, SGI wake-up of the PSCI workers, the PL011 receive
        interrupt, and that the GIC, CPU interface and timer state after the
        handoff teardown equals the state before kShimC touched it. Used by
        tools/test_qemu_irq.py.
